# Docs, example tests and skill stay in sync with the code

This is a required rule, not a suggestion. `test/ArchitectureTests/DocumentationConsistencyTests.cs` enforces the structural part in CI.

## When a change touches usage

A change in `src/` that affects how the library is used (public API, behavior, registration, returned error types, defaults, namespaces) updates three things in the **same pull request**:

1. the affected consumer page under `docs/guides/` (or `docs/product/package-selection.md`, `docs/product/driver-escape-hatches.md`, `docs/security/production-mongodb.md`);
2. that page's example test (`test/*/Examples/`), whose fixture summary names the page with `Proves docs/<path>.md`;
3. the consumer skill `skills/using-dilcore-mongodb` (rules and decision tables in `SKILL.md`, `references/examples.md`, `references/docs-index.md`).

Adding, renaming or removing a page also updates `docs/guides/README.md`, `skills/using-dilcore-mongodb/references/docs-index.md` and every inbound link. If nothing about usage changed, say so in the pull request.

## Page template

Every consumer page has, in this order: a title, one sentence with the purpose and the package name, then `## Setup` (complete registration with usings), `## Use` (commented snippet), `## Handle failures` (typed errors), `## Pitfalls`, `## See also`. At least one `csharp` block compiles as written and is proven by an example test that runs it against a real MongoDB.

## Content rules

- Consumer pages stand alone. They do not mention milestones (`M3`, `M4`), `PublicAPI` files, Context7 or the skill. Planned work is labelled "planned" and links to the ROADMAP.
- Types, namespaces and signatures are checked against `src/` (with Serena), never written from memory. Usings name the declaring namespace.
- The skill is used outside this repository. It links only to absolute GitHub URLs or to files inside the skill folder, and it stays tool-neutral (Context7 is optional).
- Example tests use NUnit and Shouldly with Arrange / Act / Assert comments, and copy the page's registration and types verbatim. They derive from `ExampleIntegrationTests` (or start a replica set when the page needs transactions).
